NAME
    cat - concatenate files to stdout

SYNOPSIS
    cat [FILE...]
    cat --advjson [FILE...]

DESCRIPTION
    Writes each FILE's contents to stdout in order. With no FILE,
    or when FILE is `-`, reads from stdin.

    --advjson mode (session 82) emits each non-empty line of the
    input as a JSONL record: {"line": "<the line text>"}. Used
    inside `|>` pipelines so downstream filters like pluck/where/
    count can operate on text files without breaking the JSONL
    convention.

EXAMPLES
    cat hello.txt
    cat /etc/passwd
    cat a.txt b.txt > combined.txt          # shell redirection
    cat /etc/passwd |> count                # how many users

EXIT STATUS
    0   every FILE was read
    1   at least one FILE could not be opened

SEE ALSO
    head(1), tail(1), wc(1), grep(1)
